Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: tuned default gamma and OV13858 black level

Carried by the SP11 image only (libcamera 0.7.2, Fedora 44 spec: add as Patch and
%autosetup -p1). Both changes are small and candidates for upstream.

1. Adjust: read an optional "gamma" key from the tuning file and use it as the
   default of the Gamma control. Stock 0.7.2 always starts at 2.2 and has no way to
   carry a sensor tuned value; a tuning file with the key still loads on an
   unpatched libcamera (the key is ignored).
2. CameraSensorHelperOv13858: provide the black level (64 at 10 bits, 4096 in the
   16 bit scale the helpers use), so the Software ISP does not guess it when no
   tuning file is installed. The tuning file value, when present, still wins.

The CameraSensorHelper for imx681 is not part of this patch: its gain law is an open
REA question (see libcamera-sp11-imx681-helper.patch.in).

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
index 9457d62..413d7c8 100644
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -822,6 +822,8 @@ class CameraSensorHelperOv13858 : public CameraSensorHelper
 public:
 	CameraSensorHelperOv13858()
 	{
+		/* Black level 64 at 10 bits (same scale as the VD55G1 helper below). */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
 		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 128 };
 	}
 };
diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.cpp b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.cpp
index 8bf39c4..ef6f174 100644
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 
 #include "adjust.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
+
 #include <libcamera/base/log.h>
 #include <libcamera/base/utils.h>
 
@@ -24,10 +26,15 @@ constexpr float kDefaultSaturation = 1.0f;
 
 LOG_DEFINE_CATEGORY(IPASoftAdjust)
 
-int Adjust::init(IPAContext &context, [[maybe_unused]] const ValueNode &tuningData)
+int Adjust::init(IPAContext &context, const ValueNode &tuningData)
 {
+	/* Optional tuned default gamma, clamped to the range of the control. */
+	const auto gamma = tuningData["gamma"].get<float>();
+	if (gamma.has_value())
+		defaultGamma_ = std::clamp(gamma.value(), 0.1f, 10.0f);
+
 	context.ctrlMap[&controls::Gamma] =
-		ControlInfo(0.1f, 10.0f, kDefaultGamma);
+		ControlInfo(0.1f, 10.0f, defaultGamma_);
 	context.ctrlMap[&controls::Contrast] =
 		ControlInfo(0.0f, 2.0f, kDefaultContrast);
 	if (context.ccmEnabled)
@@ -39,7 +46,7 @@ int Adjust::init(IPAContext &context, [[maybe_unused]] const ValueNode &tuningDa
 int Adjust::configure(IPAContext &context,
 		      [[maybe_unused]] const IPAConfigInfo &configInfo)
 {
-	context.activeState.knobs.gamma = kDefaultGamma;
+	context.activeState.knobs.gamma = defaultGamma_;
 	context.activeState.knobs.contrast = std::optional<float>();
 	context.activeState.knobs.saturation = std::optional<float>();
 
diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.h b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.h
index 49c1f26..fcb87d6 100644
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.h
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/adjust.h
@@ -43,6 +43,8 @@ public:
 
 private:
 	void applySaturation(Matrix<float, 3, 3> &ccm, float saturation);
+
+	float defaultGamma_ = kDefaultGamma;
 };
 
 } /* namespace ipa::soft::algorithms */
